Tighten mod-playerbots' LFG/BG queue-fill polling from 35s/30s/20s down to
10s/10s/8s, plus lower AiPlayerbot.LfgDungeonBotFillSec from 15s to 5s
(config-only, see modules/playerbots.conf).
Touches: modules/mod-playerbots/src/Bot/RandomPlayerbotMgr.cpp

Why: 2026-08-21 request to have bots fill LFG/BG queue demand "as fast as
possible". The detect-and-fill pipeline already existed end to end
(CheckBgQueue/CheckLfgQueue -> EnsureQueueFillBots -> FillLfgRaidGroup/
BGJoinAction) but was gated behind polling intervals stacking to nearly a
minute of worst-case latency before the first bot action. This only
shortens those intervals; no new logic.

--- a/modules/mod-playerbots/src/Bot/RandomPlayerbotMgr.cpp
+++ b/modules/mod-playerbots/src/Bot/RandomPlayerbotMgr.cpp
@@ (bot-fill polling call sites)
-        if (time(nullptr) > (BgCheckTimer + 35))
+        if (time(nullptr) > (BgCheckTimer + 10))
             sRandomPlayerbotMgr.CheckBgQueue();
-        if (time(nullptr) > (LfgCheckTimer + 30))
+        if (time(nullptr) > (LfgCheckTimer + 10))
             sRandomPlayerbotMgr.CheckLfgQueue();
@@ RandomPlayerbotMgr::EnsureQueueFillBots()
-    if (lastFill && now < lastFill + 20)
+    if (lastFill && now < lastFill + 8)
         return;
